  "why": "The statement is about finitely generated projective modules (vector bundles) over A[t1..tn] for every regular Noetherian A. Classical results (Murthy, Quillen-Suslin, Lindel, Rao 1988, Popescu 1989) each settle restrictions and are cases, journal-published; none settles the whole. Rao 1991 concerns unimodular rows/stably free modules and is treated as a variant. The torsor papers (Balwe-Sawant, AHW, Fedorov, Cesnavicius, Guo-Liu, Stavrova) answer the generalised question for reductive-group torsors; their GL_n specialisations land inside cases already known (equal characteristic, smooth over valuation/Dedekind rings, dimension <= 2), so for this statement they are variants, not new cases. The close call is Guo-Liu: if its GL_n specialisation over smooth algebras over non-discrete valuation rings is new for vector bundles it could be a case, but the record says Guo-Liu themselves cite the vector-bundle case over regular rings over Dedekind rings as already resolved, and the GL_n hypothesis was not checked. Popescu 2018 v1 and Banerjee 2022 are author-withdrawn. Chakraborty-Sharma has a year-only 2024 date and no established content. No AI involvement in any event.",
